  "text": "Recipe: Kale Chips\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Snack\nIngredients: nutritional yeast, pumpkin seeds, sunflower seeds, cashews, turmeric powder, pepper powder, red chili powder, garlic cloves, roasted red pepper, dates, smoked paprika, kale, Apple Cider Vinegar, mustard seed powder\nCooking methods: blend, bake\nInstructions: SPICE RUB: Grind these together: 1/2 cup nutritional yeast, 1/2 pumpkin seeds, soaked in water for 10-15 minutes [alternatives: sunflower seeds or cashews], 1 tsp turmeric powder, 1/4 tsp pepper powder, 1 Tbsp red chili powder, 4-5 garlic cloves, 1 big roasted red pepper, 4-5 dates, 1-2 tsp smoked paprika. KALE CHIPS: Wash 2 bunches of kale. Remove the ribs. Break kale leaves with hands and massage them with 1-2 tsp ACV (Apple Cider Vinegar). Then coat them with Spice Rub and bake them at 325 F for 30-35 minutes, checking in between. Then sprinkle 1 tsp freshly ground mustard seed powder on kale chips.\nNotes: TIPS: (1) To make them crispy, apply less Spice Rub. (2) Adjust the level of spiciness with less or more chili powder.",
